{
  "name": "route-folding-across-loop-iterations",
  "semantics": "baseline",
  "description": "A while-loop shape: stage-1 and stage-2 route twice (two iterations). The LAST routed entry per stage decides the final walk: stage-1 -> stage-2, stage-2 -> stage-3. The effectful step s1 ran in both iterations (two effect_completed entries); baseline folds the FIRST delta. Resume address empty once the last routes break the cycle.",
  "definition": {
